摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Codex-style Computer Use for DeepSeek Harness: the official window2 13-method desktop surface plus Chromium automation, a visible overlay with Esc interrupt, per-app approvals and bundled skills. Windows, MIT, no Codex required.","id":"gh:1371041124","install_available":true,"language":"Python","name":"dsh-computer-use_codex-style","slug":"wushi2333/dsh-computer-use_codex-style","topics":["codex","computer-use","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","rust","windows-automation"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Codex-style Computer Use for DeepSeek Harness: the official window2 13-method desktop surface plus C"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"hromium automation, a visible overlay with Esc interrupt, per-app approvals and bundled skills. Wind"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ows, MIT, no Codex required."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Computer Use for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Drive Windows desktop apps and Chromium tabs from DeepSeek Harness.**\n**Based on the Codex `window"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"2` tool surface** — **the Codex-style Computer Use experience on DeepSeek Harness.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"*As of this plugin's release, the official harness has shipped Computer Use in an experimental relea"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"se, with a noticeably different design. This plugin is coexistence-safe: both can be installed side "},{"id":"p5s3","text":"by side, but running both drivers at once is not recommended.*"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- What you get\n- Quick start\n- How it works\n- Tool surface\n- The act-and-refresh loop\n- Safety model"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"\n- Experience layer\n- Configuration\n- Browser automation\n- Verification\n- Build from source\n- Reposi"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"tory layout\n- Troubleshooting\n- Security and privacy\n- Compatibility and known gaps\n- License and at"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ut\n- Troubleshooting\n- Security and privacy\n- Compatibility and known gaps\n- License and attribution"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## What you get"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| **The full Codex surface** | All 13 official Codex `window2` methods — `list_windows`, `get_window"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"`, `list_apps`, `launch_app`, `get_window_state`, `click`, `press_key`, `type_text`, `scroll`, `set_"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"value`, `drag`, `perform_secondary_action`, `activate_window` — with the same names, parameters, def"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"aults, return shapes and error strings as Codex. |\n| **Real input, real screenshots** | `SendInput` "},{"id":"p9s5","text":"for input, UI Automation for the accessibility tree, `Windows.Graphics.Capture` for screenshots that"},{"id":"p9s6","text":" work even when the window is occluded. Screenshots arrive as vision image parts, never as base64 in"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"side JSON. |\n| **A visible, cancellable overlay** | A status pill plus an animated synthetic cursor."},{"id":"p9s8","text":" The pill is hidden for the duration of each screenshot, so the model never reads its own status pil"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"l back while you keep seeing it. **Esc** interrupts the turn at any moment. |\n| **Verified against t"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"he real thing** | Behaviour is gated against the official plugin and its helper: AX tree grammar, ov"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"erlay pixels, cursor motion, capture freshness, transport budgets, approval strings, turn lifecycle."},{"id":"p9s12","text":" |\n| **Harness-native, not MCP-shaped** | DSH tools with a bundled skill, not a JavaScript REPL. The"},{"id":"p9s13","text":" plugin is a DSH **bundle**: `package.json` + `cordis.patch.yml` + entry modules at the package root"},{"id":"p9s14","text":". |\n| **Two planes, one sidecar** | The desktop is process-wide, so the pointer, overlay, capture an"},{"id":"p9s15","text":"d approvals live on the HOST plane; the model-facing tools live in an agent preset, so an ordinary c"},{"id":"p9s16","text":"oding session never gets the mouse. |\n| **An experience layer** | Local, machine-specific notes writ"},{"id":"p9s17","text":"ten after a task and replayed as advisory context before the next one — see Experience layer. |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### Requirements"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| OS | Windows 10 1809+ or Windows 11, **x64** |\n| Harness | DeepSeek Harness (a source checkout or "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"an installed `dsh` CLI) |\n| Node | 20 or newer |\n| Python | 3.10+ — only for the optional browser ca"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"talog; the 13 desktop tools are Rust + Node |\n| Rust | only if you rebuild the helper (a release bin"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ary already ships in `helper-rs/bin/win32-x64/`) |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### 1. Install the bundle"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The bundle declares `dsh.bundle.patch`, so `dsh plugin` adds the HOST-plane row to the profile and l"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"inks the package. The plugin is plain ESM JavaScript plus a prebuilt helper, so it ships **no `prepa"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"re` or `postinstall` script** — pnpm never asks you to allow a build."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### 2. Add the tool row to an agent preset"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The desktop tools deliberately live in an **agent preset**, not in the host composition. Pick the pr"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"eset you want to give the mouse to and add one row to its `agent.cordis.yml` (presets live in `$DSH_"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"HOME/.agent-presets/<name>/`):"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Keep a separate preset for Computer Use if you prefer: sessions started with the `standard` preset t"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"hen keep their normal tool set and never touch your mouse."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### 3. Deliver the skills"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The two skills ship inside the package and are copied into the skill roots the harness reads:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\nsh\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-computer-use"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\nmermaid\nflowchart TB\nsubgraph DSH[\"DSH profile\"]\ndirection TB\nsubgraph HOST[\"HOST plane"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" — process-wide\"]\nS[\"dsh-computer-use\nService `dshComputerUse`\npointer · overlay · capture · approva"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"ls\nturn lifecycle · experience store\"]\nend\nsubgraph PRESET[\"PRESET plane — one agent preset\"]\nT[\"dsh"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"-computer-use/tool\n13 window2 tools\n+ harness extensions\"]\nK[\"skills\ncomputer-use · computer-use-bro"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"wser\"]\nend\nS <-->|\"JSON-RPC over stdio, one JSON object per line\"| H[\"dsh-computer-use.exe\nRust help"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"er\"]\nH -->|SendInput| APP[\"target Windows app\"]\nH -->|UI Automation| APP\nH -->|Windows.Graphics.Capt"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"ure| APP\nT --> S\nP[\"Python engine (optional)\nCDP · Playwright · browser catalog\"] <--> S"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]\nmermaid\nsequenceDiagram\nparticipant M as Model\nparticipant C as Computer Use\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Security and privacy"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- **The agent controls the real mouse, keyboard and screen.** Run Computer Use in a session where th"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"at is acceptable, and keep the deny list intact.\n- **Approvals are explicit.** `launch_app` and audi"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"o recording can pause for the harness approval UI; nothing is approved silently, and a refusal is ne"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"ver retried.\n- **The experience store is local and bounded.** It lives inside the plugin folder, is "},{"id":"p27s5","text":"gitignored, is never packed, and never records typed text, element names or screenshot bytes.\n- **Sc"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"reenshots are vision parts.** They travel to the model as image attachments; the JSON tool result ca"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"rries no base64.\n- **Untrusted content stays untrusted.** Pages, documents and mail can inform the m"},{"id":"p27s8","text":"odel but cannot authorise an action."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Compatibility and known gaps"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The plugin targets the Codex Computer Use plugin baseline `26.903.61454`: same 13 methods, same para"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"meter names and defaults, same return shapes, same error strings, same AX tree grammar, same budgets"},{"id":"p29s3","text":", same overlay semantics."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The official DSH Computer Use follows a noticeably different design. Use this plugin when you want t"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"he Codex-style behaviour."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
